@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+Feature: Editing todos
+  As a user
+  I want to edit existing todo titles
+  So that I can correct or update my tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+    And the user has added a todo "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a todo enters editing mode
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" should have the editing class
+    And the edit input for "Buy groceries" should be visible and focused
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit by pressing Enter
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user changes the edit input to "Buy organic groceries"
+    And the user presses Enter
+    Then the todo "Buy organic groceries" should be visible in the list
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" should not be visible in the list
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit on blur
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user changes the edit input to "Buy fresh groceries"
+    And the user blurs the edit input
+    Then the todo "Buy fresh groceries" should be visible in the list
+
+  Scenario: Trimming whitespace from edited title
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user changes the edit input to "  Buy fresh groceries  "
+    And the user presses Enter
+    Then the todo "Buy fresh groceries" should be visible in the list
+
+  Scenario: Empty edit destroys the todo
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user changes the edit input to ""
+    And the user presses Enter
+    Then the todo list should contain 0 items
+
+  Scenario: Escape discards edit changes
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user changes the edit input to "Something else"
+    And the user presses Escape
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" should be visible in the list
+    And the todo "Something else" should not be visible in the list
