+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+Feature: Persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to survive page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my task list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Todos persist across page reload
+    And the user has added a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is completed
+    When the user reloads the page
+    Then the todo list should contain 2 items
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" should be visible in the list
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" should have the completed class
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" should be visible in the list
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" should not have the completed class
+    And the active count should be 1
+
+  Scenario: Persistence uses localStorage key "todos-vanillajs"
+    And the user has added a todo "Test persistence"
+    Then localStorage should contain a key "todos-vanillajs"
+
+  Scenario: Empty todo list on fresh state
+    Then the todo list should contain 0 items
+    And the "#main" section should be hidden
+    And the "#footer" section should be hidden
