@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+Feature: Routing and filtering
+  As a user
+  I want to filter my todos by status
+  So that I can focus on active or completed items
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+    And the user has added a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is completed
+
+  Scenario: Default route shows all todos
+    When the user navigates to "#/"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" should be visible in the list
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" should be visible in the list
+    And the "All" filter should be selected
+
+  Scenario: Active filter shows only active todos
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the todo "Walk the dog" should be visible in the list
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" should not be visible in the list
+    And the "Active" filter should be selected
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" should be visible in the list
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" should not be visible in the list
+    And the "Completed" filter should be selected
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a todo in filtered view updates the list
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Walk the dog"
+    Then the todo list should contain 0 items
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    Then the todo "Walk the dog" should be visible in the list
+
+  Scenario: Active filter persists on reload
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    And the user reloads the page
+    Then the "Active" filter should be selected
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" should be visible in the list
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" should not be visible in the list
+
+  Scenario: All filter selected by default
+    When the user navigates to "#/"
+    Then the "All" filter should be selected
diff --git a/features/toggling-todos.feature b/features/toggling-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4377ab6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/toggling-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+Feature: Toggling todo completion
+  As a user
+  I want to mark todos as complete or active
+  So that I can track which tasks are done
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+    And the user has added a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: Clicking a toggle marks a todo as completed
+    When the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" should have the completed class
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" checkbox should be checked
+
+  Scenario: Clicking a toggle on a completed todo marks it as active
+    Given the todo "Buy groceries" is completed
+    When the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" should not have the completed class
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" checkbox should be unchecked
+
+  Scenario: Mark all as complete checks all todos
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then all todos should be completed
+    And the toggle-all checkbox should be checked
+
+  Scenario: Mark all as complete unchecks all when all are completed
+    Given all todos are completed
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then no todos should be completed
+    And the toggle-all checkbox should be unchecked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all reflects individual toggle state
+    When the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox should be unchecked
+    When the user toggles the todo "Walk the dog"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox should be checked
+
+  Scenario: Active count updates when todo is toggled
+    Then the active count should be 2
+    When the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the active count should be 1
+    When the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the active count should be 2
diff --git a/features/visibility.feature b/features/visibility.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d08f811
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/visibility.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+Feature: Section visibility
+  As a user
+  I want the app to show only relevant sections
+  So that the interface stays clean
+
+  Background:
+    Given the todo app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Main and footer hidden when no todos
+    Then the "#main" section should be hidden
+    And the "#footer" section should be hidden
+
+  Scenario: Main and footer shown when todos exist
+    When the user has added a todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the "#main" section should be visible
+    And the "#footer" section should be visible
+
+  Scenario: Active count displays correctly
+    When the user has added a todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the active count should be 1
+    And the active count label should be "item"
+    When the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    Then the active count should be 2
+    And the active count label should be "items"
+
+  Scenario: Active count does not include completed todos
+    When the user has added a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is completed
+    Then the active count should be 1
